    "durationMs": 177562,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `database/migrations/2026_11_22_000000_create_links_table.php` — links table with unique `code`, `url` text, `clicks` defaulting to 0, timestamps\n- `app/Models/Link.php` — Eloquent model with an integer cast on `clicks`\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — create, show, redirect, and list endpoints; generated codes via `Str::random(8)` with collision retry; duplicate custom codes return 409 (pre-checked plus a SQLSTATE 23000 catch for races)\n- `routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php` — routes registered with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links`, `/r/{code}` exactly; JSON renderables for 422 (validation), 404, and 405\n- `start.sh` — runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `php artisan serve --no-reload --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000` in the foreground, preserving the provided `DB_*` env vars (nothing hard-coded; env overrides the starter's sqlite `.env`)\n- README rewritten with a \"Starting the server\" section and full API reference\n\n**Testing** — I exercised every requirement against the running server via curl: 201 creation with generated/custom codes, 409 duplicates, 422 for malformed JSON, missing/invalid URLs (`ftp://`, `https://` with no host), and codes that are too short/long or contain bad characters; 302 redirects with the exact `Location` and exactly-one click increment; list ordering and totals; and 404 JSON errors. Data and click counts survived a full server restart (MySQL verified via Boost's schema tool). I also caught and fixed a return-type bug that broke `GET /r/{unknown}`, removed a default-throttling risk by confirming the api group has none, ran Pint (clean) and the test suite (passing), then wiped my test rows and stopped the dev server so the automated suite starts fresh."
  }
